The temporary SVG is appended to `document.body` for measurement but is only removed on the happy path. If `configureLabelImages` or the bounding box measurement throws an exception, `tempSvg` will never be removed, leaking a hidden `<svg>` element into the document. Wrap the measurement block in a `try/finally` to guarantee cleanup:
```js
try {
  await configureLabelImages(div.node(), node.label);
  // ... bbox measurement ...
} finally {
  tempSvg.remove();
}
```
